==German==

===Etymology===
Probably related to Indo-European ''*sker-a-'' "to [[cut]]", which is related to [[scheren]]. Akin to English {{m|en|shard}}, Old Norse {{m|non|skarð||notch, hack}} ( > Danish {{m|da|skår}}).

